            <ArticleTitle>Therapeutic uses of contraceptive steroids.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>315-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During the past 20 years, contraceptive steroids have undergone significant changes as the result of an increased understanding of their metabolic, pharmacologic, and hormonal activities. During this time, prospective and retrospective epidemiologic studies have elucidated several noncontraceptive health benefits of oral contraceptive steroids, including their therapeutic effects for endometriosis, dysmenorrhea, polycystic ovarian disease, and benign breast disease. From this review it appears that the benefits of oral contraceptive steroids in young, healthy, nonsmoking women far outweigh their more publicized, infrequent risks.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
